                <pb facs="0720" n="638" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg638"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/3314: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-09-13T14:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">September 13,
                                1925—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:27
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>142. Captain Wyman of the <hi rendition="#italic">Denver</hi> and three aides
                    arrived in Managua today. The President expresses grateful appreciation.
                    Situation proceeding satisfactorily.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
